      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i've been reading some stuff that suggests the whole structure of the UN is actually kind of broken and outdated because of that veto power you mentioned. do historians see the UN as a fundamentally flawed institution that needs a total overhaul, or do they mostly view these issues as just the inevitable reality of how global politics works?",
