      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many scholars argue that the veto power is a fundamental design flaw that hobbles the UN in modern geopolitical realities, leading to persistent calls for reform. Some view it as an outdated artifact of the 1945 power structure, making the institution inherently unsuited for a multipolar 21st-century world. However, others argue that, given the current distribution of power, radical overhaul is politically impossible, so the UN is best understood as a flawed but necessary compromise.",
